# Windows application and taskbar branding
Workstream-ID: lea-32
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/32
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded Windows application-icon request
Status: DONE
Milestone: Use the project mark for desktop windows and Windows executables
Dependencies: lea-11, lea-12

## Purpose
Replace generic interpreter branding with the existing seafoam application-form
and lightning mark. Give Windows a stable application identity without changing
saved settings, editing the interpreter or disturbing a running application.

## Tasks
- [x] Inspect desktop startup, existing artwork and executable packaging.
- [x] Prepare an independent public-source candidate and preservation baseline.
- [x] Add a multi-resolution Windows icon and stable desktop taskbar identity.
- [x] Embed the same mark in both Windows executables.
- [x] Qualify native window branding, icon resources and affected regressions.
- [x] Update the directly affected guide and retain exact candidate evidence.
- [x] Retain one issue-backed Project item and persistent backlink.
- [x] Integrate and qualify the combined, separately authorized source-publication lane.
- [x] Promote the qualified candidate at a coordinated source-app save point.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] The actual project mark renders clearly at small and high-DPI icon sizes.
- [x] Desktop startup sets a version-independent Windows identity before Qt startup.
- [x] Non-Windows startup remains supported; native identity failures are explicit.
- [x] Source desktop, tutorial and packaged desktop entries share the icon setup.
- [x] Both executable definitions embed the multi-resolution icon resource.
- [x] Fictional checks preserve running applications, settings and released assets.
- [x] Candidate qualification is not reported as activation, acceptance or release.
- [x] One issue-backed Project item and durable backlink represent the workstream.
- [x] Source promotion is verified without disrupting the independent application.

## Completion evidence
Exactly eight isolated candidate payloads implement shared startup branding,
the affected guide and regressions. The existing original mark supplies nine
ICO sizes from 16 through 256 pixels. All 82 affected cases, Black/Ruff and
mypy pass. A real Windows check verifies the explicit application identity,
both hidden-window native icons and all nine exact embedded frames in both
newly built executables. Extracted executable icons match the original exactly;
actual native renders are visually reviewed. Frozen offline smoke confirms
the application icon, desktop rendering, tutorial and real sibling CLI.

The original binary-inclusive patch first passes read-only applicability without
changing the active checkout. That earlier checkpoint preserves its 175 public
preimages, selected private/native metadata, both original candidates and eight
installed entrypoints. Publication remains distinct from runtime activation.
The subsequent source-only authorization promotes the complete qualified commit
ac06298f8aed81a74df195399e9c88ed78b333f9 into original main after checking the
full Windows interpreter/process tree and absence of an active GUI/application
run or dashboard client. Existing dashboard process identities remain unchanged.
No cache/pin manipulation, independent restart, live qualification, human
acceptance or new release is claimed.

A separately authorized source-publication lane combines the eight branding
payloads with the no-note candidate into twenty-nine files. The two overlaps
merge cleanly and the remaining twenty-seven payloads match their original
frozen candidates exactly, including the ICO. All 253 combined affected cases,
repository Ruff, Black over 119 files and mypy over seventy-three modules pass.
Retain all thirty earlier workstreams and reconcile only these two descriptions.
Commit/remote/hosted read-back is separately complete; publication itself did
not switch the original checkout, replace an installation or move a tag.
The distinct local promotion now verifies original-source imports, the unchanged
launcher's nonlaunching check and eleven focused fictional regressions, including
all nine source icon sizes and shared startup. Private/native metadata, unrelated
work and unchanged source preimages are preserved. The installed application is
explicitly excluded: no update, launch, replacement or uninstall is performed.

